#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6456693-8845-5f7b-8b0b-2d6802bbf72e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Constant Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3977d627-65bc-5f36-8c25-7d47b515f383" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3566" :question/problem "Given that $p(x)=9x^4$ and $q(x)=3x^4$, what is $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -\\infty} \\dfrac{p(x)}{q(x)}$?" :question/worked-solution "When we divide the two functions, we get a constant, and the limit of a constant is just the constant itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → - ∞)(p(x))/(q(x)) &= lim_(x → - ∞)\\frac{9x^{4}}{3x^{4}} \\\\\n&= lim_(x → - ∞)3 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4974097a-95c9-5835-ba1d-46480efab66b" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Power Function With an Even Power"}] :question/id #uuid "88c456d9-e5d3-5b33-a847-03f201751c19" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-36" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} \\left(-12x^{12}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "The graph $y=x^{12}$ looks similar to an upward parabola, so\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} x^{12} = \\infty\n$$\n\nHowever, multiplying by the negative coefficient $-12$ causes $y=-12x^{12}$ to look more like a downward parabola. This changes the sign of the limit. Therefore,\n\n$$\nlim_(x → ∞)(-12x^{12}) =-lim_(x → ∞)(x^{12}) = - ∞\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5bea806-2913-57f5-ba32-be7aeda5bd15" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Power Function With an Odd Power"}] :question/id #uuid "551f2aa0-8589-5725-abe6-de1b7eca0327" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-37" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow -\\infty} \\dfrac{x^3}{2}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → - ∞)\\frac{x^{3}}{2} &= lim_(x → - ∞)(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot x^{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot lim_(x → - ∞)x^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=x^3$ is power function with an odd positive power and therefore has the property that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to-\\infty} x^3 = -\\infty\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the positive constant\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\ndoes not affect the limit at infinity. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot lim_(x → - ∞)x^{3} &= lim_(x → - ∞)x^{3} \\\\\n&= - ∞\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105499 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc04f720-28f3-55ab-8e89-582db57672a4" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a General Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "969d5f07-c5ce-5601-b2de-0d23eb15809b" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-39" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{y\\rightarrow -\\infty} (44-3y^4-9y^{12}) \\,$." :question/worked-solution "We identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(y → - ∞)(44 - 3y^{4}- 9y^{12}) &= lim_(y → - ∞)(-9y^{12}) \\\\\n&=-lim_(y → - ∞)(y^{12}) \\\\\n&= - ∞\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5bea806-2913-57f5-ba32-be7aeda5bd15" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Limit at Infinity of a Power Function With an Odd Power"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "844e69f5-bf0e-5220-a337-129f2e7b58c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- ∞" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103746} {:answer/id #uuid "86e72c35-b802-51d7-9b81-24285d48f52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "DNE" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103747} {:answer/id #uuid "c8385ccd-d194-5907-87a1-4f1d2235b281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∞" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103748} {:answer/id #uuid "cafe89ee-461c-5362-875a-1eca2b94a01f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103749} {:answer/id #uuid "f4119f9f-bb91-5151-b690-05e3804a4893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8385ccd-d194-5907-87a1-4f1d2235b281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∞" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103748} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade21269-3eba-5437-a026-e6edf7ec7052" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186103745}] :question/id #uuid "7c7529a5-2ffe-53f0-9bca-cd9b5d97a802" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-35192" :question/problem "Evaluate $lim_(x → - ∞)(-\\frac{x^{5}}{4})$."}]}
